    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16">

                <pb facs="0120" n="20" xml:id="pg20"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 General Committee/781: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-02-17T12:00:00+01:00">February 17,
                            1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received February 17—9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. Point of view of Foreign Office, also reflected in the press, is that French
                        <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> of February 14<anchor n="57"
                        xml:id="d16-f1"/> published here yesterday constitutes no advance whatever
                    in Franco-German armament negotiations.</p>
                <p>No reply will be made till after visit of Eden who is expected here Monday
                    evening.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodd</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d16-f1" n="57" xml:id="d16-f1-content">
                <p>For English text of French <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>, see Great
                    Britain, Cmd. 4559, p. 3.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
